= Introduction
The CLEC Project continues to spearhead educational advancement through targeted capacity-building initiatives. This formal impact assessment report evaluates the forthcoming "Digital Literacy & AI Integration Workshop," scheduled to run from November 1, 2026, to November 5, 2026. This initiative is designed to equip educators with essential digital competencies and pedagogical strategies for integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) into contemporary educational frameworks.

= Objectives
The primary objectives of the workshop include:
- Enhancing the digital literacy of participating educators across multiple districts.
- Providing foundational knowledge and practical skills for AI integration in classroom settings.
- Fostering a collaborative network among educators from diverse educational institutions.
- Awarding 2 credit course units to successfully participating teachers to support their professional development.

= Methodology
This assessment utilizes a mixed-methods approach, relying on quantitative enrollment data from the CLEC database and projected qualitative feedback mechanisms. The data encompasses participant demographics, institutional representation, and geographical distribution to ensure a comprehensive evaluation of the program's reach and anticipated impact.

= Geographical Overview
The workshop has successfully drawn participation from a diverse array of geographical regions, ensuring a broad dissemination of the pedagogical strategies discussed. 

